WEBVTT

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:35.130
Taeguk refers to the source of everything in the universe and the universal law in which

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:43.230
everything continuously goes through cycles of creation and destruction.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:50.430
Taeguk paljang stands for gom and symbolizes the source of growth.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:57.090
Taeguk paljang is also a pumsae that summarizes the basics and represents mature techniques

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:07.350
of Taekwondo when moving on from an initiate to becoming a belt holder.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:02:20.040
We will now take a look at the pumsae of Taeguk paljang.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:30.280
Taeguk paljang consists of six key moves, namely dubal dangseongjagi, kkoduro bakkadmakgi,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:48.070
waesan dulmakgi, dangyeo jirugi, kkoduro aramakgi, and ddiyeo apjagi.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:52.430
These are the six key moves of Taeguk paljang.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:59.040
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Taeguk paljang.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:04.680
Dubal dangseongjagi is a kicking technique where you jump and perform two midair

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.540
kicks in succession.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:14.000
The first balchagi lightly kicks the target at the torso level, and the second balchagi

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:20.890
kicks a target higher with the other foot.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:30.480
Koduro bakkadmakgi is a technique to block with your hands with help from the assisting hand.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:37.210
The fist blocking the torso should be placed at the solar plexus level,

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:44.480
while assisting hand is placed level with the blocking elbow.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:50.240
Be careful not to let the blocking hand move outside the outer line of the body.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:56.640
Do not let the assisting armpit detach from the body.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.720
Weesan dulmakgi is a technique where your arms are crossed in front of your chest.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:10.000
The inner arm blocks the lower body, and the outer arm performs olgul anpalmok bakkadmakgi.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:17.000
The wrist of the arm performing anpalmok olgul bakkadmakgi should be level with the philtrum,

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:24.680
while the arm performing aremakgi should be about two raised fists apart from your adjacent leg.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:30.520
The elbow of the arm performing anpalmok olgul bakkadmakgi should face downward.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:37.520
The eyes should point in the direction of the arm performing arebakkadmakgi.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:47.510
Tangyo jirugi is a technique used mostly to strike the chin by pulling an opponent's clothing.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:54.120
The jirugi starts at the chest line with the fist pulled back.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:05:03.620
The fist performing jirugi passes by the wrist being pulled back and reaches the target.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:11.760
Be careful not to let the hammer fist touch the front of the shoulder performing jirugi.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:21.730
Also, be careful not to let the fist start at the back and perform jirugi upward, like chichirugi.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.810
When performing godoro aremakgi,

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:31.850
the blocking hand should maintain a space of two raised fists above the knee set forward.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:40.760
The assisting hand should be level with the elbow that performs aremakgi.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:49.700
Dio-aptagi is a technique used to jump and perform aptagi mid-air.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.700
The kick must complete at the peak of your jump.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:06:02.970
These are the six key moves of taeguk paljang.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.970
We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.970
The key moves of taeguk paljang first part consist of

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.960
When connecting from the first move,

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:38.960
you must perform the preparatory move of pulling the right fist back.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:45.970
After the first kick of ddubal dangseong chagi,

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:55.030
bend your kicking leg, then continue with the next balchagi.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:07:00.030
Prepare for the wen anmakgi once your right foot touches the ground.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:06.030
Quickly connect with wen anmakgi and double jirugi the moment your left foot touches the ground.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:13.460
Cautions for taeguk paljang first part, taking a closer look.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:18.460
Shout the moment you perform the second balchagi during ddubal dangseong chagi.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.110
Do not pull your right fist back and perform jirugi

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:31.110
when connecting from wen goduro bakkadmakgi to momtong jirugi.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:41.630
We will now practice the moves of taeguk paljang first part in succession while watching the video.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:55.610
The key moves of taeguk paljang second part consist of

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:38.020
The first performing jirugi should face upward and placed between your solar plexus and chest line.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:45.020
Then pulling arm should be free from unnecessary force and placed level with the shoulder line.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:49.020
Twist your torso and pull your arm.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:53.020
Then slowly perform dangyo jirugi by exerting force.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.060
Shift your weight to your right foot.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:09:02.060
Then pass your left foot in front of your right foot to assume the apkoasagi posture

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:08.080
when connecting to wen sonar godura makki.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:13.080
After performing dangyo jirugi, shift your weight to your left foot.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:20.080
Spin your body 90 degrees counterclockwise, then pull your right foot backwards.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.080
After performing orun apchagi,

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:28.120
return the kicking leg to where it was before the kick like you're reclaiming it.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:33.360
Then set your left foot one step backward.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:38.640
Immediately pull your right foot towards your left foot,

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.640
then perform orun bomseogi and orun battangson anmakgi.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:49.310
Cautions for taeguk paljang second part, taking a closer look.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:53.560
When performing weisan teulmakgi,

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:57.560
your feet should stand diagonal to punsae's progress line.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:04.540
Be careful not to disconnect the moves that connect apchagi

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.540
to mullo didyeo battangson anmakgi.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:13.200
We will now practice the moves of taeguk paljang second part

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:16.200
in succession while watching the video.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:51.760
The key moves of taeguk paljang third part consist of

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:54.760
wen sonar godura makki,

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:58.760
wen apchagi and orun jirugi,

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.760
wen battangson anmakgi,

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.800
orun sonar godura makki,

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.800
orun apchagi and wen jirugi,

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.800
and orun battangson anmakgi.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:16.200
Perform anchagi and jirugi in succession.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:21.770
Move the body center back transition to bomseogi,

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.770
then perform anmakgi.

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.770
Slowly repeat after me.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:30.790
Shift your weight to your front leg

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:35.790
and at the same time spin your torso clockwise using your left ball.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:41.790
Then perform the preparatory orun sonar godura makki move.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:46.130
Complete the sonar godura makki move by spinning

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:50.130
and setting the left foot in the direction of progression.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:54.570
Cautions for taeguk paljang third part,

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.570
taking a closer look.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.570
When spinning and setting your foot from the wen bomseogi

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.570
to orun bomseogi,

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.570
do not overset your right foot

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:07.570
and spin your torso with your fixed left foot.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:13.880
Such turns stiffen the body and can cause injury to the knees.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:16.880
You must understand the coordination between

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.880
moving the center of the body

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.880
and spinning the torso when performing dikki and doradikki.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:28.800
We will now practice the moves of taeguk paljang third part

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.800
in succession while watching the video.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:50.010
The key moves of taeguk paljang fourth part consist of

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:53.010
godura are makki,

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:55.010
wen abchagi,

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:57.010
orun diyo abchagi,

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.010
orun an makki,

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:02.010
double jireugi,

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.010
wen sonar bakat makki,

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:08.840
orun palkumchi doryeochigi,

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:11.840
orun ddeungjumeok abchigi,

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.840
wen jireugi,

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.840
orun sonar bakat makki,

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:19.840
wen palkumchi doryeochigi,

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.840
wen ddeungjumeok abchigi,

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.840
and orun jireugi.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:28.970
After wen abchagi,

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:29.970
bend your knee,

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:31.970
jump with your right leg,

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.970
and continue with the orun diyo abchagi.

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:43.010
Shout at the same time while performing orun diyo abchagi.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:48.890
Land after performing diyo abchagi.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:53.890
Then naturally connect to an makki and double jireugi.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:57.890
Open your chest while performing palkumchi doryeochigi.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:01.890
Then target the area slightly above the shoulder.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:05.890
Turn the torso that twisted during palkumchi doryeochigi

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:07.890
to the opposite direction

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.890
and continue with ddeungjumeok abchigi.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.890
Then use the movement of the pelvis

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.890
to complete the move with jireugi.

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:21.490
Concentrate on the coordination of the three moves.

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:27.310
Cautions for daegeuk paljang, fourth part,

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.310
taking a closer look.

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:33.310
When performing diyo abchagi,

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.840
be careful not to perform abchagi

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.840
by relying on the rebound from the front kicking foot

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.840
moving up and down.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:48.270
We will now practice the moves of daegeuk paljang,

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:51.270
fourth part, in succession while watching the video.

00:14:51.270 --> 00:15:11.270
This concludes training for daegeuk paljang.

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:14.270
The only thing remaining is to become a belt holder.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:19.860
We will take another look at all the moves

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.860
and master pumsae.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:16:35.320
We have looked at the key moves of daegeuk paljang

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:38.320
and provided thorough explanations for each move

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:41.320
and things to watch out for.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.320
As you are now on the verge of becoming a belt holder,

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.320
continue with devotion and the proper mindset

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.320
to better grasp the postures and techniques.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:55.630
We will see you again in the koryo video.

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.630
Thanks for watching.

